      "Choosing to step into the unit exactly as it runs today, choosing to modernise it with newer automation and export capability, or choosing an independent engineering career instead are three genuinely different decisions with real income and relationship consequences - not one obvious answer",
      "Getting this right, instead of drifting into the family unit out of habit or walking away without a plan, is what actually moves you toward earlier financial freedom",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "You are inside PSG Tech, Amrita, or a similar Coimbatore engineering programme and the pressure is already building",
    listItems: [
      "PSG College of Technology and Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham anchor a genuinely strong engineering education base in Coimbatore, feeding directly into the city's own pump, textile-machinery, and auto-component manufacturers rather than only into distant metros",
      "That proximity is an advantage, but it also narrows the default script early - core-manufacturing placement, a family unit, or a smaller TIDEL Park IT role rarely get compared honestly against each other before a decision gets made",
      "A high-value skill portfolio built around design, quality, automation, or export operations can unlock high income opportunities across any of those three routes - but only if someone actually maps the comparison instead of taking whichever offer arrives first",
    ],
  },
  {
    title: "A generic career pep talk will not untangle a precision-manufacturing family decision",
    listItems: [
      "Generic \"just join the family business\" or \"just get into an MNC\" advice skips the real trade-offs a pump, textile-machinery, or auto-component unit actually carries",
      "You need someone who can weigh Coimbatore's actual industrial base, your family's specific situation, and your own risk tolerance honestly, not a script written for a services-IT city",
      "You want one practical next step for your unit, your branch, or your TIDEL Park option - not a motivational line that could apply to any tier-2 city",
    ],
  },
];

const coimbatoreContextItems = [
  {
    title: "CRI Pumps, Texmo Industries, and Kirloskar Brothers make Coimbatore a genuine, globally significant pump-manufacturing cluster",
    body: "Coimbatore is widely known as India's Pump City, and the name is earned - CRI Pumps and Texmo Industries were both built and are still headquartered here, alongside a major Kirloskar Brothers manufacturing presence, feeding an export market that reaches well beyond India. Around those anchor names sits a dense layer of smaller foundries, casting units, and precision-component suppliers that most people outside the industry never hear named, but that together form one of the world's genuinely significant pump and pump-component manufacturing bases. For a large share of Coimbatore families, this is not an abstract industry - it is the family's own unit, a relative's workshop, or the employer three streets away.",
  },
  {
    title: "Lakshmi Machine Works and the textile-machinery trade give Coimbatore a second, equally real manufacturing identity",
    body: "Lakshmi Machine Works (LMW), headquartered in Coimbatore, is one of the largest textile-machinery manufacturers in the world, and it sits inside a wider ecosystem of textile-spinning-equipment and ancillary-component makers that grew alongside Tamil Nadu's own textile mills. This is a genuinely different manufacturing identity from pump-making - more spinning-and-weaving-equipment engineering than fluid-handling engineering - and a family or individual rooted in this trade faces its own version of the same succession and modernisation questions, distinct from a pump-manufacturing household's version.",
  },
  {
    title: "Pricol and Roots Industries add a real auto-components layer to the same industrial base",
    body: "Coimbatore's precision-engineering strength also extends into automotive components - Pricol and Roots Industries both have a major manufacturing presence here, supplying instrumentation, horns, and other components into India's wider auto industry. For engineering graduates and families whose work already touches machining, tooling, or quality control, this auto-component layer is often a closely related option to the pump or textile-machinery trade rather than a separate industry entirely, widening the real comparison a Coimbatore family actually needs to make.",
  },
  {
    title: "PSG College of Technology and Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham feed this base directly, which cuts both ways",
    body: "PSG College of Technology is one of Tamil Nadu's most respected engineering institutions, and Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham's Coimbatore campus adds a second strong anchor, together producing a steady pipeline of mechanical, production, and instrumentation engineers who often join Coimbatore's own manufacturing base rather than leaving for a metro. That local absorption is a genuine advantage most tier-2 engineering hubs do not have, but it also means the honest comparison against a metro product-company role, a TIDEL Park IT job, or higher studies rarely gets made carefully before a decision is locked in by proximity alone.",
  },
  {
    title: "TIDEL Park is a real but genuinely smaller IT corridor here, not a competing claim on Chennai's scale",
    body: "Coimbatore's own TIDEL Park and a smaller surrounding IT-and-ITES presence give the city a real technology-sector option alongside its manufacturing base. It is worth naming honestly rather than ignoring, but it remains a secondary, smaller-scale corridor compared with Chennai's OMR IT belt or Bangalore's technology economy - and treating it as an equal-sized alternative to Coimbatore's own globally significant pump and textile-machinery manufacturing base would misread the city's actual economic weight.",
  },
];

const pumpSuccessionItems = [
