  {
    title: "RS Puram, Race Course, and the PSG Tech and Amrita campus belt hold the professional and academic population",
    body: "RS Puram, Race Course, and the areas around PSG College of Technology and Amrita's Coimbatore campus carry a meaningful population of salaried professionals, second-generation business families, and students weighing higher studies against direct entry into the family trade or a manufacturing employer. Someone from this side of the city is often one step removed from the shop floor itself, comparing a corporate, research, or higher-studies path against inherited business expectations rather than facing the operational succession question directly.",
  },
];

const objectionItems = [
  {
    title: "My family expects me to join our pump, foundry, or textile-machinery unit - is stepping away even a real option?",
    body: "It is a real option, and so is staying while changing how the business runs. The honest first step is evaluating the specific unit - its real order book, its export readiness, and whether your own strengths fit running or modernising it - rather than treating the decision as loyalty versus ambition. Either path can move toward earlier financial freedom if it is chosen deliberately rather than by default.",
  },
  {
